# StockLedger demo story. Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension and JetBrains IDEs:
# open this file and click "Send Request" above each block, top to bottom.
# Expects a freshly seeded database (ids below: keyboard = product 1, Warehouse A = warehouse 1).
# Reset: docker compose down -v && docker compose up -d db, then restart the API.

@base = http://localhost:3000
@key = dev-demo-key

### 1. Find the keyboard (reads are public, no key needed)
GET {{base}}/products?query=keyboard

### 2. Receive 15 keyboards into Warehouse A
POST {{base}}/stock/receipts
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: {{key}}

{ "productId": 1, "warehouseId": 1, "quantity": 15, "reference": "PO-1001" }

### 3. Available stock is now 15
GET {{base}}/inventory?warehouseId=1&sku=KB-001

### 4. Order 4 keyboards -> 201, stock is deducted in the same transaction
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: {{key}}

{ "warehouseId": 1, "externalReference": "SHOP-5001", "items": [{ "productId": 1, "quantity": 4 }] }

### 5. Available stock is now 11
GET {{base}}/inventory?warehouseId=1&sku=KB-001

### 6. Order 20 -> 409 INSUFFICIENT_STOCK, nothing changes
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: {{key}}

{ "warehouseId": 1, "items": [{ "productId": 1, "quantity": 20 }] }

### 7. The ledger: receipt +15 and order -4, with timestamps and references
GET {{base}}/stock/movements?productId=1

### 8. Same externalReference again -> 200 with the existing order, no second deduction
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: {{key}}

{ "warehouseId": 1, "externalReference": "SHOP-5001", "items": [{ "productId": 1, "quantity": 4 }] }

### 9. Order list (paginated)
GET {{base}}/orders?page=1&pageSize=10

### 10. Cancel the order -> stock goes back to 15 with a compensating +4 movement
POST {{base}}/orders/1/cancel
x-api-key: {{key}}

### 11. Cancel again -> 409 ORDER_NOT_CANCELLABLE
POST {{base}}/orders/1/cancel
x-api-key: {{key}}

### 12. A write without the key -> 401
POST {{base}}/stock/receipts
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": 1, "warehouseId": 1, "quantity": 1, "reference": "no-key" }

### 13. Invalid payload (negative quantity) -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{base}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
x-api-key: {{key}}

{ "warehouseId": 1, "items": [{ "productId": 1, "quantity": -1 }] }
